#+TITLE: cador: entget of a main-space entity has no 330 owner; header group order differs from AutoCAD
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: cador-entget-pointer-codes-are-handle-strings
#+BRANCH:

* Symptom

Found while fixing =cador-entget-pointer-codes-are-handle-strings=
(clautolisp 2.3.7), on the clautolisp baseline run of
=probes/sources/probe-entget-pointers.lsp=:

#+begin_src lisp
(setq l (entmakex '((0 . "LINE") (8 . "0") (10 0.0 0.0 0.0) (11 1.0 1.0 0.0))))
(assoc 330 (entget l))   ; nil on cador; AutoCAD: (330 . <*Model_Space record>)
#+end_src

and the header order of entget differs:

- cador LINE: =-1 5 0 ...= (handle before type)
- cador XRECORD after dictadd: =-1 5 330 0 100 280 ...= (the owner is
  inserted after the FIRST stored group, which is the 5)
- AutoCAD (documented examples): =-1 0 5 [102 {ACAD_REACTORS 330 102 }] 330 100 ...=

* Cause

=clautolisp.drawing:add-entity= stores =(5 . handle)= at the head of the
data; the owner of a main-space entity is implicit (=entity-handle-block=
NIL) and only written as a 330 by the DXF writer (=dxf.lisp=, the
=*Model_Space= record handle); =set-entity-owner= (dictionary.lisp) puts
the 330 after the first group.

* Fix sketch

Synthesize the 330 owner in the AutoLISP view (the block record's id as an
ENAME -- table record ids are gensyms in a fresh cador document, so they
need a real handle first), and order the view's header groups
=-1 0 5 [102...] 330 100= like the vendors. TO MEASURE against the
=entget-pointers= probe results (LINE in model space, XRECORD codes)
before relying on the exact order.
